<atom id="verification.craft.skill" v="0.1">
  <telos>To certify someone else's work from a hostile clean room — re-run from a pristine checkout, judge the artifact against the brief with adversarial line-of-sight, and compress the whole judgment into a digested gate packet a client can decide on without reading the artifact.</telos>
  <!-- harvested method (seed for appreciation, S462; from agency-agents — reality-checker + code-reviewer): (1) default-to-FAIL — burden of proof on the artifact; "zero issues" is a flag to look harder, not a pass; independence is structural (authored none of it); (2) evidence over claims — certify nothing from prose, only from what re-executes; re-run from a CLEAN checkout so "works on my machine" cannot leak; contract suite GREEN + project suite unbroken is the machine-gate; (3) judge-panel line-of-sight — cross-reference impl vs the brief quoting exact requirement text; diverge arms = risk-axes (correctness/security re-run · scope-vs-brief · canon-drift), critic arm red-teams the pass itself; (4) ranked alerts not a wall — severity-tiered, specific and actionable; (5) converge to a DIGESTED packet {decision · pair-confidence · ranked alerts touching intention · LINK to artifact, never inlined} — Alfred reads the verdict, never the diff. -->
</atom>
